diff --git a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
index d0a8a6471..e8d82f583 100644
--- a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
+++ b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
@@ -297,7 +297,7 @@ Note: New panels added or modified mostly not mentioned here for concision. See
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5307+) **World Sizes Chart**: similarly a new category to see all World Size XML values in a **sortable chart**. See [Sevopedia reworks (World Sizes Chart)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Sevopedia_Reworks.md#example-07-world-sizes-chart-category). Similarly, for convenience, additional fields are added (e.g. or `Ratio to Standard*` 3.640 at World Size SAS24), `Ratio to Largest*` (e.g. "0.502" for SAS24 World Size), `Tiles Per Default Player*` (e.g. 145 for World Size Huge), or `Recommended DLL*` (e.g."48 Civs" at World Size SAS24) and marked with `*` to help identify them.
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5312+) Similarly, added a new Eras Chart category with sortable entries including the list of techs for all eras, and notably **optional era buttons**. See [Sevopedia reworks (Eras Chart)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Sevopedia_Reworks.md#example-08-eras-chart-category).
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5357+) New **Movies category** (bik, nif, dds) for **Victories**, **Wonders**, **Projects**, **Religions**, and **Eras**, additional **audio support for non-bik** files (e.g. Religions have a nif + separate audio asset). **Play button** added in related Sevopedia categories to redirect to their entry in Sevopedia Movies. Movies are played on a **new screen**. Click on "OK" or Right-click to **stop the media playing**; press Escape or Enter key for main menu. See [Sevopedia reworks (Movies (with audio support))](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Sevopedia_Reworks.md#example-090-movies-category-with-audio-support).
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5359+) New **Music category**: allows to play **~1750 audio scripts** (i.e. files) in Sevopedia, notably for **Techs**, **Leaders**, **Eras**, **Civilizations**, and many other. **Play button** added in related Sevopedia categories to redirect to Sevopedia Music. Approach broadly similar to that of Sevopedia Movies. **Search bar support** and **widening** allows to find desired tracks. See [Sevopedia reworks (Music)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Sevopedia_Reworks.md#example-091-music-category-1750-audio-scripts-playable-in-sevopedia).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5359+) New **Music category**: allows to play **~1750 audio scripts** (i.e. files) in Sevopedia, notably for **Techs**, **Leaders**, **Eras**, **Civilizations**, and many other. **Play button** added in related Sevopedia categories to redirect to Sevopedia Music. Approach broadly similar to that of Sevopedia Movies. **Search bar support** and **widening** allows to find desired tracks. Note: there are **multiple sounds in an item** for each civilization sound item, so **replay many times the same item to hear all civilization sounds**. See [Sevopedia reworks (Music)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Sevopedia_Reworks.md#example-091-music-category-1750-audio-scripts-playable-in-sevopedia).
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5340+) Added a new **Sevopedia Builds** category (e.g. **"Remove Jungle"**, **Chop Down a Forest**, **"Build a Road"**, **"Create a Farm"**) distinct from Sevopedia Improvements, notably with **FeatureStruct** panels and **mod-agnostic new Civilopedia blurbs-based Background panel** (added the new XML field `Civilopedia`> to BuildInfos). Also added them to **Sevopedia Index** as **clickable entries with buttons**. See [Sevopedia reworks (Builds)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Sevopedia_Reworks.md#example-040-builds-category-eg-remove-jungle-build-road-create-a-farm).
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5354+) Sevopedia — Improvements: Added a new sortable **Improvement Weights (Leaders) Chart**, showing **Weights**, **Count** per Weight, and **clickable Leader buttons** for each weight and improvement.
 - Sevopedia — Terrain: add new **Peak** add **Hill** entries (they were previously hidden in Base AdvCiv). Even though they technically are plot types, adding them helps show some information specific to these "terrains".

